{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l23fa8ax","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"chemical-bonding-and-molecular-structure","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"hybridization-and-vsepr-theory","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pthe-shape-of-xeosub2subfsub2sub-molecule-isp-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-zkjb2termapjpygb","content":"<p>The shape of XeO<sub>2</sub>F<sub>2</sub> molecule is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"trigonal bipyramidal."},{"identifier":"B","content":"square planar."},{"identifier":"C","content":"tetrahedral."},{"identifier":"D","content":"see-saw."}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>The electronic configuration of Xe is 5s<sup>2</sup> 5p<sup>6</sup>; and that of Xe in excited state is 5s<sup>2</sup> 5p<sup>5</sup> 5d<sup>1</sup>. The hybridisation is sp<sup>3</sup>d and geometry is see-saw. The actual shape is trigonal bipyramidal but due to the preaence of lone pair it gets distorted to see-saw structure.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l26hvc85/3fb52983-347e-4e04-8f07-796b439d3623/a355ed50-c010-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hvc86.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l26hvc85/3fb52983-347e-4e04-8f07-796b439d3623/a355ed50-c010-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hvc86.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Chemical Bonding &amp; Molecular Structure Question 17 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l26hvc85/3fb52983-347e-4e04-8f07-796b439d3623/a355ed50-c010-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hvc86.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l26hvc85/3fb52983-347e-4e04-8f07-796b439d3623/a355ed50-c010-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hvc86.png?format=png 750w, ht